+# INP diagnostics
+
+The page loads a local, unmodified copy of Google's `web-vitals` 6.2.3 attribution
+build (Apache-2.0, license in `scripts/vendor/web-vitals.LICENSE`). Source release:
+https://registry.npmjs.org/web-vitals/-/web-vitals-6.2.3.tgz.
+No CDN or build step is needed.
+
+Set the `inp-report-endpoint` meta tag in `index.html` to an existing analytics
+collector URL to receive JSON POST bodies via `sendBeacon`, with a keepalive
+fetch fallback. The collector must accept `text/plain` JSON. This static app
+does not provide a collector; no network reports are sent until one is configured.
+Allow the collector in your CSP `connect-src` policy if applicable.
+
+To inspect reports locally, add `?inp-debug=1` to the page URL and enable debug
+messages in the console. Alternatively, subscribe to the `inp-report` window
+event and read `event.detail`.
+
+Each report includes INP in milliseconds, its rating, interaction target/type,
+page load state, and its three phases:
+
+- High `inputDelay`: investigate work already blocking the main thread.
+- High `processingDuration`: investigate interaction event handlers.
+- High `presentationDelay`: investigate rendering, style/layout and paint work.
+
+Where supported, `longestScript` identifies the script URL, function, character
+position, forced layout time, overlapping phase and duration. These are diagnostic
+clues, not proof of causation. Without Long Animation Frames support this field is
+`null`; INP phase reporting still works. Browsers without Event Timing support
+do not report INP. No interaction means no INP measurement.
+
+Reports arrive when the INP candidate changes and when the library finalizes a
+measurement on page hide. Upsert the latest value by metric `id` rather than
+counting every update as a separate page visit. The library handles restoration
+from the back/forward cache. Reports include good interactions too, for comparison.
+Page and script URL query strings/fragments are excluded. Default interaction
+selectors can contain element IDs/classes, so avoid putting sensitive data in
+those attributes.
+
+Run automated checks with `npm test`. No browser is required.
